-- title:
--   Hecke-module ladder, cube-free levels, auxiliary level r
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$; $p$ is a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ (hypotheses `hp2`, `hp𝒪`). The datum $\bar\rho$ is a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k$: a $k$-vector space of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to its endomorphisms which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite subextension of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$; `habs` asserts that the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\overline k$ has no proper non-zero invariant subspace. Two finite sets of naturals $S\supseteq S_{\min}$ are given with all members of $S$ prime (`hS`, `hSmin`), $p\in S_{\min}$ (`hpSmin`), and `hmin`: a prime $q\neq p$ lies in $S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, ramification at $q$ meaning that some valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q\in P$ non-invertible has an inertia element acting non-trivially.
--
--   A ladder of levels is given by $n\in\mathbb N$, a sequence $N_k=\mathrm{Nf}\,k$ of non-zero naturals and a sequence $q_k=\mathrm{qf}\,k$. The level hypotheses are: `hNS`, every prime divisor of any $N_k$ lies in $S$; `hNp`, for $k\le n$, $p^2\nmid N_k$ and $p\mid N_k\iff p\mid N_n$; `hNmin`, for $k\le n$ every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N_k$; `hNunr`, for $k\le n$ a prime $q\neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $N_k$ divides it to exponent at least $2$; `hN3`, for $k\le n$ and every prime $q\neq p$, $q^3\nmid N_k$; `hfoot`, $N_n$ is squarefree and every prime $q\neq p$ dividing $N_n$ lies in $S_{\min}$; `hrung`, for $k<n$ the number $q_k$ is a prime in $S$ with $q_k\neq p$, and exactly one of $N_k=N_{k+1}q_k^2$ with $q_k\nmid N_{k+1}$, or $N_k=N_{k+1}q_k$ with $q_k\mid N_{k+1}$ and $q_k^2\nmid N_{k+1}$, or $N_k=N_{k+1}q_k$ with $q_k^2\mid N_{k+1}$, holds.
--
--   The hypothesis `hihara` is an Ihara-type statement imposed at each rung $k<n$ with $q_k^2\nmid N_{k+1}$, for every $\mathcal O$-module $A$, every non-zero $\ell_0$ and every $M$, equipped with degeneracy data $h_1,h_q$ of type [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) $M\ (Mq_k)\ \top\ \top\ 1$ and $\ldots\ q_k$ and their analogues $h_1',h_q'$ one step higher (such a `LevelLE` datum records $M\mid M'$, $d\mid M'/M$ and compatibility of the unit subgroups, here both taken to be $\top$). Under the assumptions $q_k\nmid M$, $A$ has no $q_k$-torsion, $\ell_0$ prime and $\ell_0\nmid Mq_k$, it requires: (a) if $g,h\in \mathrm{H}^1(M,\top;A)=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(M,\top),A)$ satisfy $i_1(g)+i_{q_k}(h)=0$, where $i_d=$ [`CohCarrier.iDeg'`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L396) is precomposition with the degeneracy map, then $g$ and $h$ are both Eisenstein at $\ell_0$, i.e. the Hecke operator $T_{\ell_0}$ acts on them as $(\ell_0+1)$; and (b) if $x,z'\in \mathrm{H}^1(Mq_k,\top;A)$ satisfy $i_1(x)+i_{q_k}(z')=0$ at the next level, then there is $w\in \mathrm{H}^1(M,\top;A)$ with $z'-i_1(w)$ and $x+i_{q_k}(w)$ Eisenstein at $\ell_0$ at level $Mq_k$.
--
--   The hypothesis `htame` requires, for every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$, that the adic representation [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) $\bar\rho$ be unipotent on inertia at $q$: at every valuation subring lying over $q$, each inertia element has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$.
--
--   The auxiliary prime is $r$, with hypotheses $r$ prime, $5\le r$, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid N_kp$ for all $k\le n$, $p\nmid r-1$ (`hr`, `hr5`, `hrS`, `hrN`, `hr1`), and `hrρ`: for every valuation subring $P$ over $r$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ (i.e. $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition group and acts as $x\mapsto x^r$ on the residue field), $(\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma))^2\neq (r+1)^2$ in $k$. Each level $N_k$ is assumed to have an integral structure in weight $2$, meaning that the $\mathbb C$-span of the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of cusp forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is all of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N_k))$.
--
--   The Hecke data are: ring homomorphisms $\theta_k=\theta_{\mathrm f}\,k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) $(N_k,2,S)$ — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N_k))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N_k$, $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N_k$, $q\notin S$ — to $k$, satisfying `hθ`: for every prime $\ell\nmid N_k$ with $\ell\notin S$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta_k(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Further, $\chi$ is a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra of level $N_n$ to $\mathcal O$ lifting $\theta_n$ (`hχ`), and for each $k$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k=\pi T\,k$ from the local Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) $(N_k,S,\mathcal O,\theta_k)$ — the localisation of the $\mathcal O$-Hecke algebra at the multiplicative set coming from the complement of the prime determined by $\theta_k$ — to $\mathcal O$, with `hπT`: for $k\le n$ and primes $\ell\notin S$ dividing neither $N_k$ nor $N_n$, $\pi_k$ of the image of $T_\ell$ equals $\chi(T_\ell)$. Finally a sequence $a:\mathbb N\to\mathcal O$ is given together with `ha`: for each rung $k<n$ with $q_k\nmid N_{k+1}$ there is a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) $\rho'$ over $\mathcal O$ (a free $\mathcal O$-module of rank $2$ with an adically continuous Galois action) whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell\nmid N_{k+1}$, $\ell\notin S$, are $X^2-\pi_{k+1}(T_\ell)X+\ell$, which is unramified at $q_k$ and whose trace at a Frobenius at $q_k$ equals $a_k$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a family of types $M_k$, each an additive group carrying a module structure over the local Hecke algebra `heckeLocal` $(N_k,S,\mathcal O,\theta_k)$ and an $\mathcal O$-module structure forming a scalar tower with it, finite and free over $\mathcal O$, together with $\mathcal O$-bilinear forms $B_k:M_k\times M_k\to\mathcal O$, such that:
--
--   (i) for $k\le n$ each $B_k$ is Hecke-self-adjoint: $B_k(t\cdot m,m')=B_k(m,t\cdot m')$ for all $t$ in the local Hecke algebra;
--
--   (ii) for $k\le n$ the map $m\mapsto B_k(m,\cdot)$ from $M_k$ to its $\mathcal O$-dual is bijective;
--
--   (iii) for $k\le n$ the submodule of $M_k$ annihilated by the kernel ideal of $\pi_k$, `Submodule.torsionBySet` with respect to $\ker\pi_k$, is non-zero;
--
--   (iv) for $k\le n$ the $\mathcal O$-rank of $M_k$ equals the product of the $\mathcal O$-rank of that $\ker\pi_k$-torsion submodule with the $\mathcal O$-rank of the local Hecke algebra at level $N_k$;
--
--   (v) for each $k<n$ there are $\mathcal O$-linear maps $i:M_{k+1}\to M_k$ and $j:M_k\to M_{k+1}$ and an element $\Delta$ of the local Hecke algebra at level $N_{k+1}$ such that $B_{k+1}(j\,m',m)=B_k(m',i\,m)$ for all $m'\in M_k$, $m\in M_{k+1}$; $j(i\,m)=\Delta\cdot m$ for all $m\in M_{k+1}$; $i$ carries the $\ker\pi_{k+1}$-torsion submodule of $M_{k+1}$ onto the $\ker\pi_k$-torsion submodule of $M_k$ (as $\mathcal O$-submodules); $\pi_{k+1}(\Delta)\neq 0$; if $q_k\nmid N_{k+1}$ then $(q_k-1)\bigl(a_k^2-(q_k+1)^2\bigr)$ divides $\pi_{k+1}(\Delta)$ in $\mathcal O$; and if $q_k\mid N_{k+1}$ with $q_k^2\nmid N_{k+1}$ then $q_k^2-1$ divides $\pi_{k+1}(\Delta)$;
--
--   (vi) under the additional assumption that $p\mid N_n$ implies that [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) $\bar\rho$ is not flat at $p$ (flatness at $p$ being the condition that the residue field is finite and that, for every ideal $I$ with $\mathcal O/I$ finite, $V/IV$ is realised Galois-equivariantly as the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring of rationals with denominator prime to $p$): there exist a proof `hc` of the commutation property [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.OpComm`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L30) $(N_n,r,S,\mathcal O)$ of the auxiliary-level operators and an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ from $M_n$ to [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.ML`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L46) $(N_n,r,S,\mathcal O,\theta_n,hc)$, the module attached to the Hecke data on the carrier $\mathrm{H}^1(\Gamma_H(N_nr),\mathcal O)$ with generating set the primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N_n$ and $\ell\neq r$, such that $e$ intertwines the two actions: for each such generator $g$ and each $m\in M_n$, $e$ applied to the action of the image of $T_{\ell(g)}$ on $m$ equals the action of the polynomial variable $X_g$ of the free algebra `MvPolynomial (Gen …) 𝒪` on $e(m)$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-module input to the Taylor–Wiles argument on a level-raising ladder: a ladder of $\mathcal O$-lattices with perfect Hecke-equivariant pairings, generic-rank and rung-congruence information at each step, and, at the foot of the ladder, an identification of the Hecke module with the auxiliary-level module built from $\mathrm{H}^1$ at level $N_nr$. It is the cube-free-levels variant, carrying the extra hypothesis $q^3\nmid N_k$ for primes $q\neq p$, and it feeds the strict-ordinary Taylor–Wiles statement at auxiliary level.
